2) Implementing Requirements
This table should serve as a draft for how you will implement the requirements into your
final project. You may change your ideas later on, but your final site must fulfill all the
requirements.
Requirement Implementation
Purpose/Functionality
A 1-2 sentence description of the
purpose or functionality of your
site
Make a watchlist of movies and mark them as
watched or unwatched to keep track of ones that
user has seen. They can also see stats like
average rating and genre.
State Dataclass Attributes
Minimum of 4 attributes, one of
which must be a list/dict of
instances of your second
dataclass.
Briefly describe each attribute, its
type, and how it will be
meaningfully modified throughout
the site.
owner_name: str: the user’s name, shown in the
greeting and changed through the name page
watchlist: list[Movie]: all movies on the list. It grows
when a movie is added, shrinks when one is
removed, and has its watched fields changed when a
movie is marked watched
movies_watched: int: how many movies are watched.
It’s recalculated with count_watched after marking or
removing a movie, and reset to 0 when the list is
cleared
status_message: str: feedback shown on pages,
such as “Added Alien!” or “Please enter a title.” It’s
updated by nearly every handler route
Second Dataclass
Your second dataclass, including
its attributes, their types, and how
they will be meaningfully modified
(if they are modified)
Movie with these attributes:
title: str: set when the movie is added and never
changed
genre: str: chosen from a SelectBox when the movie
is added
rating: int: 1 to 5, converted from the SelectBox string
when the movie is added
watched: bool: starts as False and becomes True in
mark_watched
Routes (minimum 7) index, name_page, save_name, add_page,
The names of your route
functions
add_movie, list_page, mark_watched,
remove_movie, stats_page, reset_list
Pages (minimum 5)
A brief description of the pages in
your site
index: home page with a greeting, status, movie
counts, and navigation buttons
name_page: form for changing the owner’s name
add_page: form to enter a title, genre, and rating for
a new movie
list_page: table of all movies, with controls to mark
one watched or remove one
stats_page: average rating, top-rated movie, watched
count, and a table of movies per genre
User Input (minimum 3)
Description of user input
components (TextBox, TextArea,
CheckBox, or SelectBox) and
their purposes
For more information on these
input types, see Drafter
Documentation.
TextBox("owner_name") on name_page: type a new
name
TextBox("title") on add_page: type the movie title.
SelectBox("genre") on add_page: pick one of the five
genres
SelectBox("rating") on add_page: pick 1 to 5 stars
SelectBox("title_to_watch") on list_page: pick which
unwatched movie to mark watched
SelectBox("title_to_remove") on list_page: pick which
movie to delete
If Statements (minimum 3)
Brief description of what will be
evaluated in your if statements
and how they will meaningfully
change the logic of the site
save_name: if the trimmed name is blank, show an
error and return to name_page otherwise save it
add_movie: if the list is full, the title is blank, or the
title is a duplicate (checked with find_movie), show
an error and stay on add_page. Otherwise append
the new Movie
list_page: if the watchlist is empty, show “Nothing
here yet” instead of the table. If there are unwatched
movies, show the “Mark as watched” controls
mark_watched and remove_movie: if find_movie
returns -1, show “Couldn’t find that movie.” Otherwise
update or remove it
stats_page: if the list is empty, redirect to add_page
instead of showing meaningless stats
Loop (minimum 1)
This loop must iterate over the
list/dict of dataclass instances in
your State attribute.
Description of this loop and why it
is meaningful to the site
In list_page, a for loop iterates over state.watchlist.
For each Movie, it builds a table row with the title,
genre, star rating, and watched status. This is how
the user sees their whole list, and it updates
automatically as movies change.
The helper functions average_rating, count_genre,
count_watched, find_movie, unwatched_titles,
all_titles, and top_movie also loop over
state.watchlist. They power the stats, the dropdown
choices, and the duplicate check
