Requirement Implementation
Purpose/Functionali
ty
Movie Night Watchlist lets a user build a personal list of
movies, giving each a genre and a 1-5 star rating. They can
mark movies as watched, remove them, and view stats such
as their average rating, top-rated movie, and genre
breakdown.
State dataclass
attributes
owner_name: str: the user’s name, shown in the greeting
and changed through the name page.
watchlist: list[Movie]: all movies on the list. It grows
when a movie is added, shrinks when one is removed, and
has its watched fields changed when a movie is marked
watched.
movies_watched: int: how many movies are watched.
It’s recalculated with count_watched after marking or
removing a movie, and reset to 0 when the list is cleared.
status_message: str: feedback shown on pages, such
as “Added Alien!” or “Please enter a title.” It’s updated by
nearly every handler route.
Second dataclass Movie, with these attributes:
title: str: set when the movie is added and never
changed.
genre: str: chosen from a SelectBox when the movie is
added.
rating: int: 1 to 5, converted from the SelectBox string
when the movie is added.
watched: bool: starts as False and becomes True in
mark_watched.
Routes (10) index, name_page, save_name, add_page, add_movie,
list_page, mark_watched, remove_movie,
stats_page, reset_list
Pages (5) index: home page with a greeting, status, movie counts,
and navigation buttons.
name_page: form for changing the owner’s name.
add_page: form to enter a title, genre, and rating for a new
movie.
list_page: table of all movies, with controls to mark one
watched or remove one.
stats_page: average rating, top-rated movie, watched
count, and a table of movies per genre.
User input (6) TextBox("owner_name") on name_page: type a new
name.
TextBox("title") on add_page: type the movie title.
SelectBox("genre") on add_page: pick one of the five
genres.
SelectBox("rating") on add_page: pick 1 to 5 stars.
SelectBox("title_to_watch") on list_page: pick
which unwatched movie to mark watched.
SelectBox("title_to_remove") on list_page: pick
which movie to delete.
If statements save_name: if the trimmed name is blank, show an error
and return to name_page. Otherwise save it.
add_movie: if the list is full, the title is blank, or the title is a
duplicate (checked with find_movie), show an error and
stay on add_page. Otherwise append the new Movie.
list_page: if the watchlist is empty, show “Nothing here
yet” instead of the table. If there are unwatched movies,
show the “Mark as watched” controls.
mark_watched and remove_movie: if find_movie returns
-1, show “Couldn’t find that movie.” Otherwise update or
remove it.
stats_page: if the list is empty, redirect to add_page
instead of showing meaningless stats.
Loop In list_page, a for loop iterates over state.watchlist.
For each Movie, it builds a table row with the title, genre,
star rating, and watched status. This is how the user sees
their whole list, and it updates automatically as movies
change.
The helper functions average_rating, count_genre,
count_watched, find_movie, unwatched_titles,
all_titles, and top_movie also loop over
state.watchlist. They power the stats, the dropdown
choices, and the duplicate check.
